LIVO2_degeneration — visual fusion degradation detection and recovery

The LiDAR-inertial-visual frontend is derived from FAST-LIVO2 by hku-mars,
Chunran Zheng and contributors. Existing author/copyright/license headers are
retained. The root LICENSE is reproduced verbatim from the upstream-derived
code distribution (GNU GPL version 2 text); this package is not relicensed as
BSD. Existing upstream headers and their commercial-contact notices are not
removed or replaced by this document.

M3DGR dataset adaptation and dataset-provided sensor parameters are attributed
to the M3DGR project (sjtuyinjie/M3DGR). Dataset files are not distributed here.

Project-specific contributions concern measurement scheduling, final visual
measurement/commit feedback, given-model service boundaries, and visual
withdrawal/probing/recovery management. The main filter state dimension and
update equations, pre-existing visual rejection and rollback are not claimed as
new contributions.

Bundled third-party source retains its own notices and licenses:
- rpg_vikit / xuankuzcr fork: package manifests declare GPLv3; GPL-3 text included.
- Sophus: Hauke Strasdat and contributors; MIT notices remain in each source.
- cv_bridge: Willow Garage, Tal Regev, scikit-image and contributors; BSD notices
  in source; src/module.hpp is Apache-2.0 (Open Source Robotics Foundation), and
  bundled Boost compatibility headers are BSL-1.0. Both full texts are included.
- compressed_image_transport: ROS perception contributors; package/source BSD.
- Livox ROS Driver2 message definitions: Livox, MIT; original LICENSE.txt retained.
- Legacy Livox ROS Driver generated type headers: Livox message definitions;
  original 2019 driver LICENSE.txt retained under include/livox_ros_driver.

The historical root LICENSE and individual third-party package licenses are
not replaced by a single blanket license statement. Attribution, repository
names, ROS wire-type names and third-party paper names are intentional naming
exceptions. See docs/THIRD_PARTY.md and third_party/SOURCES.json.

Packaging changes in this release (2026-10-12): independent ROS package and
message namespace, standalone dependency build wrappers and runtime paths.
Upstream source changes carry their original authorship; project change records
are kept separately from the third-party license texts.
